    "description": "## Summary\n\nWhenever qualifying activity occurs (v1: a completed Sign-Up), the related Player's Last Activity Date updates to the most recent activity date — through one reusable subflow that every current and future activity source calls.\n\n## Context\n\nBUILD-178's status automation runs off Account.Last_Activity_Date__c — the date of the player's most recent qualifying activity. The definition of \"qualifying activity\" will grow (today: completed Sign-Ups; later possibly redeposits or CMS logins). To keep future sources from each re-implementing date logic, exactly one subflow owns writes to this field.\n\n## Current state\n\nAccount.Last_Activity_Date\\__c (Date) exists on the Player Person Account, with help text referencing the 90-day threshold — nothing populates it. Sign-Ups link to Players via Sign_Upc.Player_\\_c.\n\n## Proposed solution\n\nNEW autolaunched subflow Player_Stamp_Last_Activity — inputs: PlayerId (Text), ActivityDate (Date). Logic: if the Player's current Last_Activity_Date\\__c is blank or older than ActivityDate → update it; otherwise no-op. The date never moves backwards. Flow description must read: \"Single writer of Last_Activity_Date_\\_c — new qualifying-activity sources call this subflow, never write the field directly.\" First caller: the BUILD-253 flow.\n\n**Date convention note.** Last_Activity_Date\\__c stays a **Date** deliberately — the 90-day threshold is a calendar-day rule, so the scheduled check in BUILD-254 compares whole days with no time-zone ambiguity. Callers converting a DateTime source (e.g., Completion_Date_\\_c) to the ActivityDate input must convert to the calendar date in the org time zone (ET); developer to verify a completion near midnight doesn't land on the wrong day.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. A newer ActivityDate (or a blank field) updates the field; an older ActivityDate is a no-op.\n2. Re-running with an identical date performs no DML.\n3. Bulk-safe when invoked from a record-triggered flow processing 200 records.\n\n## Output\n\nSubflow deployed in Partial SB; API name + registered-caller list recorded on this ticket; requirements doc updated.",
